Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:21:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] Reject unsupported numeric FP8 reductions while
 retaining byte copies

The low-level NCCL wrappers map Float8 storage to uint8 for copying, but
reduction entry points previously reused that mapping as a numeric dtype.
Reject Float8 in the three numeric reduction wrappers before communicator
creation; broadcast and gather keep their byte-copy behavior. Add a device
generic regression test for those refusals.

The filtered native gfx1013 RCCL profile excludes FP8 reduction kernels.
ProcessGroupNCCL now checks the tensor's actual HIP device before admitting
FP8 based only on the library version. Other devices retain their existing
version checks and byte-copy collectives remain unchanged.

Test Plan:
Source inspection establishes the byte/numeric mismatch; no multi-GPU
wrong-result reproduction is claimed from the single-device board. Targeted
static/format checks pass. Independent pip-only native build and guarded GPU
refusal/copy/ordinary-dtype regressions are pending and recorded in workspace
evidence after qualification.

```sh
PYTORCH_LINT_SKIP_CODEGEN=1 uv run --offline --no-project --python 3.12 --with spin==0.18 spin lint -- -a --take=CLANGFORMAT,NEWLINE,INCLUDE,RUFF,FLAKE8,PYFMT,TESTOWNERS,TEST_HAS_MAIN torch/csrc/cuda/nccl.cpp torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/ProcessGroupNCCL.cpp test/distributed/test_nccl.py
```

